WEBVTT

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:00.638
It's not like there are ordinary people
and then there are these geniuses

00:03:00.662 --> 00:03:04.991
who have this special ability
to do extraordinary things,

00:03:05.015 --> 00:03:08.115
that genius is actually something
that comes from the outside.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:09.725
Talk about that.

00:03:09.749 --> 00:03:12.601
EG: Well, I want to start by saying
that when you describe

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.314
my ideas about creativity
as being unusual,

00:03:15.338 --> 00:03:16.506
I agree with you,

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:18.952
but only to the extent
that they are unusual

00:03:18.976 --> 00:03:21.127
only very recently in history.

00:03:21.151 --> 00:03:24.179
My ideas about creativity
are actually very classical,

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:26.649
and they're very normal,
and they're very human

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:30.495
for how human beings regarded creativity
for nearly all of human history